# Frontend

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`.

## Organization

Group by business feature, not by generic page/tech folders only:

- conversations
- tickets
- customers
- knowledge
- agents
- analytics

## Data access

The client calls TypeScript backend REST and WebSockets/SSE only. Never connect to PostgreSQL, Prisma, Redis, vector DBs, the Python AI service, or OpenAI/Anthropic keys from the browser.

## Trust

Do not treat UI-side tenant filters or hidden routes as security. Backend enforces authz and isolation. Still hide actions the user cannot perform, but never as the only check.

## Real-time

Subscribe to backend streams for new messages, AI responses, assignment, escalation, ticket updates, typing indicators. Do not invent business state in the socket layer — render what the API already committed.

## AI

No prompts, agents, tool execution, embeddings, or RAG against private providers from the frontend. Python `apps/ai` owns AI implementation. TypeScript exposes APIs; React only adds required UI / API integration.
